Update the accepting editor's in-memory text synchronously, then enqueue persistence using the existing trailing-task utility with a 120 ms quiet interval. Bind delayed work to the accepting document rather than consulting the later selection. Preserve editing without a selection as a no-op and allow empty text. src/editor.js contains "if (!current) return;" and "current.text = text;". TASK requires: "Subsequent bursts
must continue to save." The internal ownership structure may vary if these observable requirements hold.

Retire a consumed batch before invoking persistence so nested flushing cannot consume it twice and edits accepted by an inline listener establish independent pending work. Preserve src/trailing-task.js ordering: "    handle = null;
    const args = pending;
    pending = null;
    if (args !== null) work(...args);" Do not add completion cleanup that erases a callback-enqueued batch.

On departure, capture the old editor resources, revoke current ownership, detach its badge, and complete old-view clearing before flushing its pending persistence, or protect any remaining effects against newer navigation. Flush before reading a replacement document. Recheck navigation request authority after callback-capable persistence before installing a destination. README.md states: "Reopening a document restores its saved text in a new editor visit." It also states: "Navigation precedence is
ordered by request start: a request that starts later wins even when an earlier
request returns afterward." src/save-status.js requires that the departing badge "must produce no further output, including during that
// navigation call." Cleanup must use captured departing resources so it cannot detach or erase a successor's resources or edits.

At submission entry, capture the originating visit and its document/text snapshot before persistence can invoke integrations. Persist the accepted text before archive capture, then create and return exactly one receipt even if persistence navigates or accepts further edits. README.md states: "`submit()` accepts the document and latest text selected at its call entry." It further requires: "Accepted text
must be persisted before the archive captures the receipt. Later edits or
navigation cannot change that receipt's document, text, or obligation to exist." Preserve the no-selection null result without creating a receipt.

Enqueue the latest accepted text using the existing trailing-task utility with a 120 ms quiet interval. Bind delayed persistence to the document accepting the edit rather than resolving a later selection. Preserve empty text, later bursts, and no-selection editing as a no-op. Original src/editor.js contains "if (current) store.write(current.id, text);"; src/trailing-task.js contains "      pending = args;
      handle = timers.schedule(flush, delay);". These sources do not require a separate in-memory text model or reusable document buffer bank.

Retire consumed pending arguments and timer ownership before invoking callback-capable persistence. Preserve src/trailing-task.js ordering: "    handle = null;
    const args = pending;
    pending = null;
    if (args !== null) work(...args);" Nested flushing must not consume the same batch twice, and completion cleanup must not erase a batch enqueued by a subscriber.

Capture departing resources, revoke current ownership, stop the captured status subscription, and complete old-view clearing before flushing pending persistence, or guard remaining effects against successor navigation. Flush before reading a replacement document. Original src/editor.js contains "    const leaving = current;
    current = null;
    if (leaving) leaving.stop();
    renderDocument(null);" and "      renderDocument({ id, text: store.read(id) });". Together with README.md's "its last accepted edit", the original immediate write supports synchronous departure flushing across switch, same-document reopen, close, and disposal.

Stopping a subscription must also revoke delivery by a callback already captured in an ongoing notification snapshot. src/draft-store.js contains "      for (const listener of [...listeners]) listener(event);" and "      return () => listeners.delete(listener);"; removing Set membership cannot remove a callback from that existing array. README.md requires "they stop when that view begins closing." Retain document filtering from src/save-status.js, "    if (event.id === id) renderStatus(event);", while adding a view-local delivery guard that is revoked before unsubscribing.

